dataset_check.body:
## What it does
Always checked: Input and Ground Truth have the same number of frames, and both images of a pair have the same resolution. With the material check on, also checked:
- frame numbers in the file names match one to one; missing numbers are listed;
- shifted frames: an Input that is closer to the Ground Truth of another position;
- Input and Ground Truth identical (the same files selected twice);
- the mean pixel difference of every pair stays within the tolerance, see [[doc:dataset_tolerance]].

## When to use
Keep it on. Shots with very large changes (background replacement, stylisation) can exceed the tolerance: raise the tolerance first, and turn the check off only when the material is known to be correct.

## Limitations
Runs only when a dataset is created. Adding a validation sequence checks its resolution and frame count only.
